#lang saffron
; saffron-dynamic-surface-pass M7: a dynamic field read on a GENERIC ADT was a
; hard compile error --
;   no type in this program has a field '.head', so a dynamic read of it can
;   never succeed
; -- because emit_dyn_field's candidate scan skipped any ADT with type
; parameters (a generic ADT has one monomorph per instantiation, and their
; field offsets differ) and, separately, any `:heap` ADT. `Cons` is both:
; `(defstruct ^heap Cons [A] (head A) (tail :int))`. So no cons list and no
; user generic struct could be read through an `any` parameter, while the
; interpreter -- which inspects the value -- answered fine.
;
; The scan now names the all-`any` monomorph, the same instantiation a dynamic
; dispatch row is keyed on and the only one a Saffron file builds, and lets the
; TAG COMPARE discriminate: a `(Duo int cstr)` box carries a different id,
; matches no arm, and falls through to `__tur_dyn_no_field`. No read is emitted
; at a guessed offset.
;
; `Duo` rather than `Pair`: `Pair` is an auto-loaded stdlib type.
;
; NOT covered, and deliberately: `(.tail l)` reads back an `int`, not a `Cons`,
; because the tail field is declared `:int` -- a type-ERASED carrier standing
; for the recursive occurrence -- so the widen boxes it with the int tag and a
; `cast` to `(Cons any)` fails. The interpreter says `Cons` there. Walking a
; cons list through an `any` therefore still does not work compiled; only the
; hard error is gone. See M7 in the report.
;
; Floats with a non-zero fractional part: each value crosses a box on the way
; out, and a truncating read would print 7 rather than 7.25.

(defstruct Duo [A B] (fst A) (snd B))

(defn hd [l] (.head l))
(defn f1 [p] (.fst p))
(defn s1 [p] (.snd p))

(defn main []
  (println (hd (list 7.25 "two")))
  (println (f1 (make-struct Duo 3.5 "x")))
  (println (s1 (make-struct Duo 3.5 "x")))
  (println (type-of (hd (list 7.25))))
  0)
